-- title:
--   First-component inclusion under a good/bad splitting over v
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, a level $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two degeneracy maps $\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}$ and $\mathrm{heckeBetaBar}$ from level $N$ to level $Nq$ over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, a place specialization $P$ for these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Let $v$ be a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ over $k$ and $S$ a set of elements of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$. Assume $q \nmid N$; every $s \in S$ lies in `R.R₁.integers`, its first residue `R.residue₁ s` lies in the valuation subring of $v$, and $s$ lies in the valuation subring of every place $W$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ W = v$ (that is, with $P.\mathrm{sp}$ of the restriction of $W$ along $\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}$ equal to $v$). Assume further that for every $\varphi$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ N$ whose image under $\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}$ lies in `R.R₁.integers` and which lies in the valuation subring of every place $u_0$ of level $N$ with $P.\mathrm{sp}\ u_0 = v$, there are $s, e \in S$ with `R.residue₁ e` not taking the value $0$ at $v$ and $\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}(\varphi)\cdot e = s$; and that $\mathrm{ChartEtaleAt}\ R\ v\ S$ holds, i.e. there are $z \in S$ and a monic $m$ of degree $q+1$ over level $N$ such that $z$ is `R.R₂`-integral with some Laurent coefficient of its second residue in a degree prime to $q$ nonzero, the image of $\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}$ together with $z$ generates everything over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, the $\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}$-image of $m$ vanishes at $z$ while its coefficients lie in the subring generated by $S$, and the derivative of that image does not take the value $0$ at $v$ at $z$. Finally let $\mathrm{good}$ and $\mathrm{bad}$ be arbitrary predicates on places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ such that every $W$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ W = v$ is good or bad, and such that every bad such $W$ admits $u \in S$ with `R.residue₁ u` not taking the value $0$ at $v$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}\ u > 0$. Then every $f \in$ `R.R₁.integers` with $W.\mathrm{ord}\ f \geq 0$ for all good $W$ over $v$ belongs to $\mathrm{chartLocalSetFst}\ R\ v\ S$: there are $g$ and $u$ in `chartClosure S`, with $u \in$ `R.R₁.integers`, such that `R.residue₁ u` does not take the value $0$ at $v$ and $f\cdot u = g$.
--
--   This is the first-component step in the local study of the fibre at $q$ of the level-$Nq$ modular function field, where the places above a place $v$ of the level-$N$ fibre are sorted into two classes and only the good ones are tested for regularity; the intended instance takes the two classes to be the places of the first and second kind of a chart. It is used in the proof of local semicontinuity on the first component and in the cusp law at infinity for a prolongation tuple.
-- source:
